--TEST--
A `Core\Response` write the checker cannot see in `Core\Task::afterResponse` work throws `LogicError` at run time, in the work and in a task it starts, and the same call in the main script does not throw -- `rule:concurrency/deferred-work-cannot-write-the-response`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The work is in a variable, so the compiler does not see the calls inside it.
// Each call changes the response, so each one throws `LogicError`.
var $work = fn(): void => {
    try {
        Core\Response::setStatus(500);
    } catch (LogicError $e) {
        echo $e->message, "\n";
    }
    try {
        Core\Response::text("late");
    } catch (LogicError $e) {
        echo $e->message, "\n";
    }
    // A task the work starts also runs after the response was sent.
    var $done = Core\Task::all({
        header: fn(): string => {
            try {
                Core\Response::setHeader("X-Shop", "1");
                return "set";
            } catch (LogicError $e) {
                return $e->message;
            }
        },
    });
    echo $done->header, "\n";
};
Core\Task::afterResponse($work);
Core\Response::setStatus(200);
echo "the response\n";
--EXPECT--
the response
A function passed to `Core\Task::afterResponse` cannot call `Core\Response::setStatus`. It runs after the response was sent.
A function passed to `Core\Task::afterResponse` cannot call `Core\Response::text`. It runs after the response was sent.
A function passed to `Core\Task::afterResponse` cannot call `Core\Response::setHeader`. It runs after the response was sent.
